# Code owners — required reviewers for the paths where a mistake is expensive.
#
# The repository ruleset already requires one approving review on every pull request. This
# narrows that for the sensitive paths: a change here needs review from a maintainer
# specifically, not from whoever is available.
#
# Chosen by blast radius, not by how often the files change:
#
#   - credentials and keys      a defect here invalidates every credential ever issued
#   - foundational adapters     the only code that touches a raw national ID
#   - residency issuance        the policy gates; each one fails closed by design
#   - consent and legal basis   what a deployment is lawfully permitted to do
#   - audit                     the record that everything else is checked against
#   - CI and release workflows  the thing that decides what "verified" and "signed" mean
#   - security and licensing    what an adopting government relies on in writing
#
# NOTE ON THE TEAM. GitHub honours a CODEOWNERS entry only when the named team has write
# access to this repository. `@Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin` holds `push`, granted for
# exactly this purpose -- without it every line below would be silently ignored and the rule
# would read as configured while never firing.
#
# So if this team is ever removed from the repository's access list, these rules stop applying
# and nothing announces it. Check `gh api repos/Harmonizedx/open-residency/teams` if a review
# that should have been required was not.

# Default: any change not matched more specifically.
*                                   @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# Credential issuance, verification, revocation, and issuer key custody.
/src/core/credentials/              @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/src/core/oid4vci/                  @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/src/core/oid4vp/                   @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# The only layer that sees a raw national ID, and the tokenization that keeps it unstored.
/src/core/foundational/             @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# Issuance policy gates and the residency record itself.
/src/core/residency/                @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/src/core/proofing/                 @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# Lawful basis for processing, and the assurance values relying parties read.
/src/core/consent/                  @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/src/core/assurance/                @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# The tamper-evident record.
/src/core/audit/                    @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# Authentication, session storage, and pairwise subject derivation.
/src/core/sso/                      @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/src/core/oidc/                     @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# The composition root: where keys, peppers and providers are wired.
/src/platform/                      @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# What "verified" and "signed" mean. A change here can weaken every check at once.
/.github/workflows/                 @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# The conformance gates themselves.
/scripts/orcs-conformance.ts        @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/scripts/mosip-conformance.ts       @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/scripts/check-license-headers.sh   @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# Commitments an adopting government relies on in writing.
/SECURITY.md                        @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/RELEASING.md                       @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/LICENSE                            @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin
/NOTICE                             @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin

# Database schema and migrations: irreversible in production.
/prisma/                            @Harmonizedx/open-residency-admin